body:
@rsanchezsaez have a look at [rendering_device.compat.inc](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/servers/rendering/rendering_device.compat.inc) and the accompanying changes in [rendering_device.h](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/servers/rendering/rendering_device.h) and it's `_bind_methods` function to see how we handle this.

It's mostly to ensure existing code in plugins and GDExtensions and such don't break (though I wonder whether that makes sense for an export plugin to worry about).

I do wonder if the rename to `_apple_platform_` will confuse people who work on MacOS instead of iOS derived operating systems. That said, I'm pragmatic, a rose by any other name is still a rose.

