body:
[BUG?] I don't think we can/should register a class twice (here and in `visionos`). And this breaks the locality of concers that a user of that class would be responsible for registering it.

So this would theoretically need to be registered in `drivers/register_driver_types.cpp`. But that would be the first GDCLASS registered there, which is also unconventional.

There's some awkwardness here, `drivers/apple_embedded/` is only included in the build when compiling for iOS or visionOS, but we need `EditorExportPlatformAppleEmbedded` always included in all editor builds (for Windows, macOS, Linux, Android and now with Xogot also iOS - and maybe eventually visionOS) so that they can have the export plugin.

That's what the hack does in `editor/SCsub`, so maybe this is best registered in `editor/register_types.cpp`, like `EditorExportPlatformPC`.

So we may want to move `EditorExportPlatformAppleEmbedded` to `editor/export/` just like `EditorExportPlatformPC`. That would also allow removing the hack in `editor/SCsub` to include `EditorExportPlatformAppleEmbedded` manually from `drivers`. But then I'm not sure what to do with `drivers/apple_embedded/export/godot_plugin_config.h`.

WDYT @bruvzg?

---

I mention a lot of different options above as food for thought. My recommendation for this PR would just be to keep it simple and do this:

